<title>GREENLAND: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>GREENLAND GOVERNMENT LIST (970421)</p>
<p>****************************************************</p>
<p>*   Note: Greenland has home rule under Denmark,   *</p>
<p>*	   which is responsible for foreign policy, *</p>
<p>*	   defence and health. A commissioner	 *</p>
<p>*	   represents the Danish government.	  *</p>
<p>****************************************************</p>
<p>			    - - - - -</p>
<p>  Commissioner.......Sten SPORRE</p>
<p>			    - - - - -</p>
<p>CENTRE LEFT-RIGHT COALITION GOVERNMENT (Formed 9 March 1995)</p>
<p>  Prime Minister.........Lars Emil JOHANSEN (S)</p>
<p>			    - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p>Culture, Education &amp; Church Affairs....Konrad STEENHOLDT (A)</p>
<p>  Economy &amp; Housing...........Daniel SKIFTE (A)</p>
<p>Fisheries &amp; Agriculture.Paviaraq HEILMANN (S)</p>
<p>  Health, Environment &amp; Research...........Marianne JENSEN (S)</p>
<p>Industry, Transport &amp;</p>
<p>Supplies....Peter GROENVOLD SAMUELSEN (S)</p>
<p>  Labour &amp; Social Affairs..........Benedikte THORSTEINSSON (S)</p>
<p>			    - - - - - -</p>
<p>  Parliament Speaker.......Knud SOERENSEN (A)**</p>
<p>						   (** Resigned 20 Apr 97)</p>
<p>			    - - - - - -</p>
<p>PARTY AFFILIATION:</p>
<p>(S) -- Siumut Party</p>
<p>(A) -- Atassut Party</p>
<p>			    - - - - - -</p>
<p>	 NOTE: Any comments/queries on the content of this</p>
<p>		 government list, please contact the Reuter</p>
<p>		 Editorial Reference Unit, London, on (171) 542</p>
<p>		 7968.</p>
<p>		    (End Government List)</p>
</text>
